en:
...I see.
You don't feel anything at all here?
Then let's try the next one.{p}

Here it is.
You've used this one too, haven't you?
Oh, or maybe you've stayed away from this restroom because it's creepy.{p}

...Oh, there's nobody in here.
I breathed a sigh of relief.
I'd been so worried there might be some monster inside that all the tension I'd been holding until then drained away at once.{p}

I can't stay in a place like this.
My sixth sense is telling me so.
I have to get out of here!{p}

...The moment I did, the restroom went silent.
I gasped for breath with my whole body.
I let out a breath so hard I thought I'd throw up my insides.{p}

Just then, the restroom door suddenly banged shut.
It sounded like someone had angrily slammed it with all their strength.
Hosoda stared hard at my face.{p}

...Behind me, I thought I could still hear the restroom door rattling.
It's my imagination.
Or else, it's just the wind...{p}

{f:Ugh|Ugh}, {f:we're pressed right up against each other... this is the worst|I should've just said no}.
{f:I|What am I} {f:hate fat people.|even doing?}
{f:And Hosoda|I don't want} {f:fits the image I have of them exactly.|to put this in any article.}
{f:He gives off this|Anyway, I don't} {f:stale, sour smell, like fat that won't burn all the way.|sense any aura at all.}
{f:Mixed with the restroom smell,|Ugh,} {f:it makes an indescribable stench.|I just want to get out of here.}
{f:And then he|Hosoda} whispered to {f:me|me}.
"Come on, {a}{f:|}, try to feel the spirits more."
Right now, the only thing I can feel is Hosoda crushing me{f:.|!}
"Mmm, I sense the spirits!
Ugh, sorry, I'm starting to feel sick!
Let's get out, quick!"
This is the only way {f:I|I} can escape from here!
"Hosoda, {f:I|I} want to get out of here, now.
Please, let's just go..."{p}

Okay, this is the restroom on the south side of the new building's first floor.
Well?
Do you feel anything here too?{p}

Actually, you know, there's a strange rumor about that last restroom.
When you said you sensed a spirit back there, for a moment I got my hopes up, wondering what was about to happen.
...Okay, here we are.{p}

A huge swarm of bugs {f:was teeming|was crawling} all over the vomit she'd thrown up.
"Shield bugs★"
The shield bugs were squirming out of the toilet tank and welling up out of the bowl.
Shield bugs give off such an awful smell that they're also called stinkbugs{f:.|, you know.}
The foul stench of the shield bugs mixed with the smell of her vomit, and {f:I|I} was about to pass out{f:.|...}{p}

"...{f:What's this|What is this}★"
Where the toilet had been until now, there was a gaping hole{f:!|!}
The hole was so black it seemed to go down forever.
"This is where we always come and go."
{f:What on earth was this guy talking about?|What in the world was he talking about?}{p}

Out of the gaping black hole, cockroaches were swarming up in a rustling mass.
They crawled out, kicking their fellows down in their scramble to be first.
Then, all at once, the cockroaches came flying at {f:us|us}.{p}

There was a man in the toilet, slithering in and out of the bowl{f:!|.}
I could tell he wasn't human.
His eyes were open wide, staring fixedly our way.
With someone else along, it {f:seems|seems} you can look at even something like this fairly calmly.
{f:The guy|The man} felt more bizarre than frightening{f:.|.}
But on a closer look, I realized the man wasn't looking at {f:me|me}.{p}

He was down on his knees before the man, bowing with his head to the floor.
Rubbing his face against the filthy restroom floor, over and over and over...
Did Hosoda know him{f:?|?}
Then the slithering man slid out of the toilet with a slurp.
For a while he hovered there, swaying{f:, and then|, and then all of a sudden}, with incredible speed, he burrowed into Hosoda's mouth{f:!|.}{p}

It looked like all the two of us could do was watch how things played out{f:.|.}
Maybe he hadn't expected things to turn out like this; Hosoda {f:seemed|seemed} to be in quite a panic.
Suddenly, that sound stopped dead.{p}

"{a}{f:|}... L-look at that!"
He pointed.
{f:I|I} looked where his finger was pointing.{p}

A woman who had hanged herself was banging against the glass, over and over again.
Through the frosted glass, her resentful eyes were staring in at us.
Somehow, we had to get out of here.{p}

{f:I|I} said to Hosoda,
"Hosoda, ram the door!"
He threw himself against the door with all his might.{p}

The lock broke, and {f:we|we} tumbled out of the stall.
{f:So we'd|It looks like we'd} managed to escape from there somehow.
At times like this, {f:a big, sturdy guy|someone like him} really comes in handy{f:.|, huh.}
{f:We|We} hurried out of the restroom into the hallway.{p}

{f:What the|What}...? A blackout{f:?|?}
It had gotten completely dark outside, so it was pitch black and I couldn't see a thing.
All I could see was the toilets glowing a pale bluish white{f:.|.}
I-is someone there{f:?|?}
From the urinals came the sound of someone relieving themselves.
This is wrong. There shouldn't be anyone in here but {f:me|me}{f:.|!}
Scared now, {f:I|I} backed away from the urinals.
Then, all of a sudden...{p}

I-it won't open...
In a panic, {f:I|I} rattled the door again and again.
But the door wouldn't open.{p}

Once they heard my answer, Hosoda and the others went back to the newspaper club room.
Whoa, looks like I really do need to go now.
I rushed into the restroom.{p}

I hurried over and opened the window.
Fresh air blew in from outside.
Ahh, what a relief. Honestly, does anyone actually clean this restroom properly?{p}

I looked toward the entrance.
...No one there.
But somehow it still felt like someone was watching me.{p}

I looked all around me.
Just as I thought, no one.
Was it just my imagination...?{p}

"Waaaaaah!"
It's going to hit me!
The instant I thought that...{p}

This time, I got out without any trouble.
I ran straight back to the club room.
.................{p}

"Hah, hah, hah, hah..."
"You sure took your time."
Inside, the seniors had been waiting, worried because I was taking so long to come back.{p}

Hosoda stood up and said to me,
"Huh? Who's that behind you?"
I spun around in a panic to look behind me.{p}

Suddenly I realized I could hear a swishing, slithering sound.
"Not again..."
Steeling myself, I raised my head.{p}

There was a finger sliding smoothly along the edge of the stall door.
It was clearly a finger reaching out from inside.
It slid along the edge of the door for a while, then suddenly slipped back into the stall.{p}

Curious, I went up to the front of that door.
"What on earth is inside..."
The instant I reached for the doorknob,{p}

Restroom and bath windows are almost always made of frosted glass.
This restroom's window was frosted glass, too.
I undid the latch and put my hand on the window frame.{p}

A pleasant breeze swept in.
As if the stagnant air were being swapped out.
Just then...{p}

"It's opening☆"
Now that I knew the door would open, I had to get out of here as fast as I could.
I threw the door open and leapt outside.{p}

"Either way I look, it's that restroom..."
I could feel all the strength draining out of my body.
And I sank to my knees right there.{p}

With my arm slung over Hosoda's shoulders, I staggered along on unsteady legs, and it seemed I had finally made it out of the restroom.
Just then, Hosoda tripped.
Of all things, he came falling toward me.{p}

"Gweh☆"
He landed on me with his entire weight.
This is exactly why I hate fat people.{p}

When I happened to look, I could see the front of a toilet bowl directly in front of me.
That's right, the part they call the splash guard.
For an instant, I thought I saw something there.{p}

"Sorry, sorry. Are you all right?"
Hosoda finally got off me.
But what was that just now...?{p}

"Eeeeeeek☆"
There was the face I had seen in the washbasin earlier.
The severed head slipped from his hand and began circling around me, slithering along and dripping water.{p}

"Now then, {a}{f:|}.
Whereabouts do you feel the aura coming from?"
Hosoda asked, coming closer to {f:me|me} than he needed to.{p}

I felt like something had crossed my field of vision.
{f:Huh|What}?
{f:I|I} strained my eyes and looked again.{p}

It felt like the black shadow moved as if to escape whenever {f:I|I} looked at a corner of the restroom.
In that case, {f:I wondered|I wondered} what would happen if Hosoda and I looked at both corners at the same time.
{f:I|I} told Hosoda about the something in the corners of the restroom.{p}

{f:I|I} told Hosoda that and started the countdown.
"Three... two... one... now!"
{f:Hosoda and I|Hosoda and I} each looked at our own corner at the same moment.{p}

Yes. That's where {f:my|my} memories of being alive end{f:.|.}
I never dreamed I'd die of a heart attack at such a young age.
Where {f:will I|will I} go after this, {f:I wonder|I wonder}?
Heaven? Or hell?
No, surely it won't be hell{f:.|, will it?}
..................
..................
...Maybe I'll just stay here in this restroom forever and ever...{p}

"Now then, {a}{f:|}.
Where are you sensing it from?
I have a rough idea myself, but I want to test your abilities, {a}{f:|}.
Come on, where?"
This was bad.
I'd only given a random answer because I didn't want to be dragged all over the school any longer.
{f:Ah, the heck with it|Oh, whatever}. It's not like Hosoda's a real psychic either{f:.|.}
If I just keep making things up, it'll be fine{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} looked around the restroom.{p}

"Huh? The urinal...?"
Hosoda seemed shaken by the unexpected answer{f:.|.}
{f:Kuh kuh kuh|Hee hee}, Hosoda's at a loss.
Since when did {f:I|I} get such a nasty personality, {f:I wonder|I wonder}?
{f:I|I} got carried away and rattled off whatever came into my head.{p}

Well, time for {f:me|me} to get out too.
It was at that very moment.
Suddenly, someone grabbed {f:my|my} collar from behind and {f:yanked|yanked} me back.{p}

{f:I|I} fearfully turned to look behind me.
...No one was there☆
{f:I|I} immediately got up and tried to dash out of the restroom.{p}

This time I saw it clearly.
A person's face was reflected in the urinal!
Steeling myself, {f:I|I} peered into the urinal.{p}

"........."
It was my own face reflected there.
W-what{f:?|?} It's just {f:my|my} face{f:...|...}
The instant I felt relief...{p}

"What's going on★"
One of the senior boys heard the noise, rushed in, and pulled {f:me|me} back from behind.
{f:I|I} was finally able to get away from the urinal.{p}

"Hosoda☆"
I rushed over and shook his body.
Then Hosoda slowly stood up.{p}

His eyes didn't seem to focus; each eyeball was pointing somewhere slightly different.
Something was wrong with Hosoda.
Suddenly terrified of his face, I tried to run away.{p}

As I was thinking that, I heard the door open, and Hosoda came back.
At that, everyone looked up.
Hosoda sat down in his chair, head hanging.{p}
